---
description: Full male name in the Kerala official form: INITIALS FIRST, then the personal name (എം. ടി. വാസുദേവൻ നായർ, ഇ. കെ. നായനാർ, എ. കെ. ആന്റണി). The initials stand for the house name and the father's given name and are never written out. Built as a <mix> over the three communities at their 2011 census shares (Hindu 54.73, Muslim 26.56, Christian 18.38) so that every row is drawn from ONE stock: the initial, the given name and the family name of a row always belong together. A config that joins ml.person.male.firstName to ml.person.lastName itself does not get that, and will emit names such as "ഫാത്തിമ ജോസഫ്" that no Kerala register contains. The Muslim branch is deliberately shorter than the other two: most Kerala Muslims carry no inherited family name at all, so two rows in three end at the given name and the rest take a house name or a lineage title (ഹാജി, തങ്ങൾ, മരയ്ക്കാർ).
generator: tdc
locale: ml
---
<mix name="p" percent="54.73,26.56">
  <case>
    <gen type="template" value="ml.person.initial"/>
    <data> </data>
    <gen type="template" value="ml.person.hindu.male.firstName"/>
    <data> </data>
    <gen type="template" value="ml.person.hindu.lastName"/>
  </case>
  <case>
    <mix percent="65">
      <case>
        <gen type="template" value="ml.person.initial"/>
        <data> </data>
        <gen type="template" value="ml.person.muslim.male.firstName"/>
      </case>
      <case>
        <gen type="template" value="ml.person.initial"/>
        <data> </data>
        <gen type="template" value="ml.person.muslim.male.firstName"/>
        <data> </data>
        <gen type="template" value="ml.person.muslim.lastName"/>
      </case>
    </mix>
  </case>
  <case>
    <gen type="template" value="ml.person.initial"/>
    <data> </data>
    <gen type="template" value="ml.person.christian.male.firstName"/>
    <data> </data>
    <gen type="template" value="ml.person.christian.lastName"/>
  </case>
</mix>
<data>${{p}}</data>
